  "productionReview": "Exact official loader.c/trampoline.c lock movement as a pair. Shared create callback takes loader_lock before instance/device-list work and releases at common cleanup/return. Shared destroy callback keeps null-handle return before acquire and unlocks at common end. Public outer locks are removed together, so normal API and direct layer callbacks share protection. Full preimage independently matches prior accepted L5 loader.c; L5 creation-chain/tail and L1 surface regions retained.",
  "supportReview": "Exact official layer.cpp/layer.h changes give each device its next GetDeviceProcAddr and introduce the GetQueue hook. Official threading case alone never calls GetQueue; its PASS cannot establish direct callback execution. An82-line supplement in the same existing threading target adds three explicit success/initialization-failure/device-memory-failure cases, no product instrumentation or new harness.",
  "testLifetimeReview": "Two persistent public owner devices in a single instance keep the top layer vector stable. Two workers perform16 GetQueue calls each; callback-created lower devices skip that layer. No concurrent vector mutation or owner destruction. ICD mutex protects count/map; observations only after joins. New-worker retry verifies reacquisition after each failure/success phase.",
